# List files or directories below to ignore them when running deploy, retrieve, push, pull, and status.
# https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.sfdx_dev.meta/sfdx_dev/sfdx_dev_exclude_source.htm
#

# --- Tooling / build noise -------------------------------------------
**/jsconfig.json
**/.eslintrc.json
**/tsconfig.json

# Manifests are not source. manifest/ sits outside packageDirectories and is never
# evaluated, so only the in-source case needs a rule.
**/package.xml

# --- Things that fight you on deploy ---------------------------------
# Profiles: usually managed per-org, or they drag in refs to metadata
# that doesn't exist in the target org
**/profiles/**

# Secrets / environment-specific
**/connectedApps/**
**/namedCredentials/**

# --- Test scaffolding you don't want in the org ----------------------
**/__tests__/**

# Documentation. LWC/Aura bundles deploy every file in the bundle folder, so a README.md
# next to a component would ship to the org. Safe for CustomMetadata: records are stored as
# *.md-meta.xml and the ignore matcher tests the full filename, so this rule does not match
# them (verified against CLI 2.138.6 with `sf project convert source`).
**/*.md

# OS noise that can land inside a metadata folder (e.g. a static resource directory)
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ---

# .sf/ and .sfdx/ - internal CLI cache dirs. They are already git-ignored and are never
# inside a package directory, so listing them here does nothing for deploy/retrieve. It
# does break "SFDX: Diff Source Against Org", which stages the org copy under
# .sf/orgs/<orgId>/remoteMetadata and resolves source components from it - a .sf/ rule
# makes that resolve to zero and the command reports "No components retrieved from org".

# **/*.ts - TypeScript is a supported LWC source format; ignoring it would drop real
# components if TS LWC is ever adopted. tsconfig.json (config, not source) is ignored above.
